estion/worked-solution "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nOur inequality contains only \"less than\" symbols. So, the endpoints $-3$ and $-1$ are *not* included. \n\n$$\n-3\\,\\,<\\,\\,x\\,\\,<\\,\\,-1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\n(-3,-1)\n$$\n\nMore formally, we can also write\n\n$$\nx\\in (-3,-1).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38fce6e7-e608-5049-89bd-6546b8fda8e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<y\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482909} {:answer/id #uuid "43f5ec63-ec14-578f-9c9b-502470b6d4f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482929} {:answer/id #uuid "6315912c-de0b-5577-9bf6-3e2c64fe43c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482985} {:answer/id #uuid "631761de-21bd-51da-88ac-879266e500a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482986} {:answer/id #uuid "d1720d90-8cb3-5638-bf04-aaa94a4aeaba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1720d90-8cb3-5638-bf04-aaa94a4aeaba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483161} :answer-field/id #uuid "d78e9d72-459d-5fce-90e1-8180676b9ebb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8242dd7c-9e76-5a08-b5a0-1fe98445b603" :question/math-academy-id "q-73902" :question/problem "The interval $y\\in [-1,2)$ corresponds to the inequality" :question/worked-solution "Every interval can be expressed as an inequality. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ to indicate that the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ to indicate that the endpoints *are* included.\n\nFor the given interval \n\n$$\n[-1,2\\,)\n$$\n\nwe note the following:\n\n- The left endpoint $-1$ *is* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $\\le \\,.$\n\n- The right endpoint $2$ is *not* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $<\\,.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality that corresponds to the given interval is \n\n$$\n-1\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,y\\,\\,<\\,\\,2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eca1adc-bc9c-5c08-a7e6-44e89120d4fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482834} {:answer/id #uuid "26a0db72-b0e4-5ff6-898c-6fbe5090f309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-5,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482880} {:answer/id #uuid "2d88ad6c-d451-5917-baac-bf77e2cf6ea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-5,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482889} {:answer/id #uuid "4b6c9f84-1d4a-5826-bc2e-d1338c645d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-5,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482945} {:answer/id #uuid "78f8e2a1-909f-520f-b506-e3974280f4b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78f8e2a1-909f-520f-b506-e3974280f4b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483023} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e0bb284-b5cb-58ef-a60f-c6b90ddcc36a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "864c6e65-68a8-5041-8665-c620b19d5bdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-28834" :question/problem "The inequality $-5\\le x<-2$ can be expressed in interval notation as" :question/worked-solution "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nFor the given inequality \n\n$$\n-5\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,x\\,\\,<\\,\\,-2\n$$\n\nwe note the following:\n\n- The left endpoint $-5$ *is* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $[\\,.$\n\n- The right endpoint $-2$ is *not* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $)\\,.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding interval is\n\n$$\nx\\in [-5,-2).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483384 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75a68108-a8cc-5fb7-90d8-d305c41c4fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7<x\\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483015} {:answer/id #uuid "943f78de-1311-5dd7-ac1a-856ec0cb4c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\le x\\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483070} {:answer/id #uuid "a18f6b94-6b53-545a-a37a-bd11450bb699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\le x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483083} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a2c334-25f5-5b4f-b754-81cc023155a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483089} {:answer/id #uuid "aefb8691-5a94-57