 *not* included.\n- Brackets ${\\color{blue}{[}}\\phantom{0} \\phantom{0}{\\color{blue}{]}}$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nThe given interval can be represented by the following inequality:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\, {\\color{blue}{\\leq}} \\,\\, x \\,\\, {\\color{red}{\\lt}} \\,\\, 2\n$$\n\nWe can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\in {\\color{blue}{[}}1,2{\\color{red}{)}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "487f9cd5-aca0-5110-a351-1c3d45518748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,7]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541573} {:answer/id #uuid "60ed0177-10a3-5141-8f0d-6b2603ad36d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,7]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541621} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f3d4df-e271-59b6-b3ae-010d04a7214b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-7,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541767} {:answer/id #uuid "d20e5b5b-a9db-58d3-92e2-e77645249c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541868} {:answer/id #uuid "eb83e406-5d7f-5868-bb88-3e5884a89c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ed0177-10a3-5141-8f0d-6b2603ad36d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,7]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541621} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e9148e1-c517-584b-81ce-f179a876160f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eee859cf-032a-5a34-a81e-4f392e60f1ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-102205" :question/problem "The inequality $0<x\\le 7$ can be expressed in interval notation as" :question/worked-solution "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nFor the given inequality \n\n$$\n0\\,\\,<\\,\\,x\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,7\n$$\n\nwe note the following:\n\n- The left endpoint $0$ is *not* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $(\\,.$\n\n- The right endpoint $7$ *is* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $]\\,.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding interval is\n\n$$\nx\\in (0,7].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd995a9-b989-5eb9-a1bd-bb739025a499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552918} {:answer/id #uuid "2f9055f6-bbd2-57f5-867f-46b21bf3bb97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552956} {:answer/id #uuid "aa39e0ad-a191-5047-bc57-3b582cadb1c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553210} {:answer/id #uuid "c6fd135d-d86a-5987-9de8-d466c75f9138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553266} {:answer/id #uuid "e83c5b5b-2113-5fab-83c6-66a9ffcc9dbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f9055f6-bbd2-57f5-867f-46b21bf3bb97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552956} :answer-field/id #uuid "37038cfb-4364-58c7-8027-27793c04b330" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "974c4026-e9d5-5cd6-80d1-e15772e57911" :question/math-academy-id "q-154717" :question/problem "The inequality $1\\le x\\le 5$ can be expressed in interval notation as" :question/worked-solution "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nOur inequality contains only \"or equal to\" symbols. So, the endpoints $1$ and $5$ *are* included. \n\n$$\n1\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,x\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\n[1,5]\n$$\n\nMore formally, we can also write\n\n$$\nx\\in [1,5].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186625840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5354141c-2574-59fc-8da7-8442f92dc043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625839} {:answer/id #uuid "5ebb1c61-cc8c-5ee0-a68c-607b480b3e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625841} {:answer/id #uuid "80d3d443-0acf-52fd-a15e-ca4f79b268d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-8,-3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625842} {:answer/id #uuid "c4cf06e1-3cce-5fa3-a142-c8ee5148c147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-8,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625854} {:answer/id #uuid "f9be6136-27b0-52cd-9f36-cdcbdb6ec133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,-3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ebb1c61-cc8c-5ee0-a68c-607b480b3e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb